Z||000002||rprevo||08-19-2000||08:34 AM|||| To obtain the title from the state of <BR>Michigan you have to get the owner to<BR>give you a reciept for the car with the<BR>vin on it with his signiture, Go to the<BR>sec of state with this stuff and they will<BR>process the paper work, The other thing<BR>that works is if the guy had an old <BR>registration they can tranfer ownership with<BR>that. If none of that is availiable they<BR>can give you a temporary permit well they<BR>(The State) search out your title.<BR>Make sure the car is not hot! Because<BR>if is they can press charges,<BR>My father did the title thing with a GTO<BR>once it's not as painfull as it sounds.<P>Ray<BR>||||reg||6
